      {
        "id": "a-taller-truss",
        "kind": "worked_example",
        "blocks": [],
        "headline": "A truss spans 6 m with its apex 4 m high, so each sloping member is 5 m long. A 24 kN load hangs at the apex. Find the force in each sloping member.",
        "lead": [],
        "reveal": [],
        "visualStateId": "",
        "workedSteps": [
          {
            "text": "At the apex two members share the load, each with vertical share rise over length.",
            "math": "2 × F × 4/5 = 24",
            "selfExplain": {
              "questionId": "engr-trusses-by-joints-9"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Solve for F.",
            "math": "F = 24 ÷ 1.6 = 15 kN"
          },
          {
            "text": "The members push down and outward on the feet, so they are in compression. The bottom member pulls the feet together, so it is in tension."
          }
        ],
        "checkQuestionId": "",
        "activityId": ""
